  "cards": [
    {
      "dot": "cyan",
      "title": "What runs in parallel",
      "items": [
        "Only the animal repath searches: moveAnimal's decisions, colonists' and raiders' searches stay serial and in place",
        "Compute marks the stage Frozen while lanes search, so lazy caches and the index self-check skip their writes",
        "Each lane has its own pathing.Searcher; a search writes only res[i]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "amber",
      "title": "Rarely engaged",
      "items": [
        "0 requests in 1,500 raid ticks and 1-3 in a 20,000-tick golden run (ARCH-010 ledger)",
        "Under 8 requests the pool runs them inline, so its workers rarely start",
        "BenchmarkAnimalRepath500: serial 1.554 ms, pool 0.980 ms"
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "violet",
      "title": "Wiring and determinism",
      "items": [
        "compose/game builds one pool per process (1 lane in captures) and passes it as Config.Pool; loads and dev scenes stay serial",
        "TestParallelEqualsSerial hashes 1, 2, 8 and shuffled lanes equal to serial every tick",
        "TestNoGoStatementsInSim bans go statements in application, domain and pkg; the pool starts the only sim goroutines"
      ]
    },
